## 1. Goals, non-goals, frozen contract

### 1.1 Goals

- G1. **New source layout** (the SPMPST layout):
  ```
  docs/
  ├── SSG.md          ← the SPMPST specification (written by Luna, P6.1)
  ├── .site/          ← all site configuration (concern files, locale bundles, public files, target files)
  ├── src/            ← all authored content: guides/ and collections/
  └── resources/      ← everything referenced by content but that is not content: assets, icons, flags, diagrams, target-bound components
  ```
- G2. Replace the monolithic, VitePress-named `vitepress.site.config.json` by **concern files** `docs/.site/<concern>.site.config.json` with **one owner per key**, plus **one locale bundle per language**. Anything VitePress-specific moves to `docs/.site/targets/vitepress.target.config.json` (opaque to the SPMPST core).
- G3. **Stop scattering language data**: language policy in one file, all per-language strings in `locales/<lang>.locale.json`.
- G4. **SSG-agnostic naming and conventions.** Config files, keys, folder names and error messages of the SPMPST core must not mention VitePress. Per-guide `vitepress.config.json` becomes `guide.config.json`.
- G5. **One shared loader** (agnostic, JS reference implementation under `scripts/spmpst/`) used by the pipeline and by the VitePress config adapter, plus a small **VitePress adapter** that turns the agnostic model + target file into the *exact legacy runtime object* the existing stage code and `site.ts` expect.
- G6. Break `source-stage.mjs`, `content-stage.mjs`, `pipeline.mjs` into named stages and shared helpers.
- G7. **Convention over configuration**: the layout is fixed by the standard (`src/guides`, `src/collections`, `resources/icons`, …) so most path keys disappear from config.
- G8. Write **`docs/SSG.md`**, the SPMPST v0.1 specification, derived from the real code behavior (section 10).
- G9. Ergonomics: `docs:new`, `docs:check`, JSON Schemas, icon names instead of duplicated `sidebar-icon.svg`.

### 1.2 Non-goals (do NOT do these in this run)

- No change to any `.vue`, `.css`, `documentation-*.ts` content except **path-only** edits forced by a file move (P5.6).
- No change to published URLs, routes, generated Markdown (except documented text-path updates, P5.6), or `.vitepress/generated/*` content.
- Do **not** implement collection category pages, concepts hover, or footer links (section 9 = design notes only).
- Do **not** write the Rust SSG. Do **not** rename `docs/vitepress-site/` (future: `docs/targets/vitepress/`).
- Do **not** rename frontmatter keys in content (`sidebarTitle`, `icon`, …). Vocabulary renames are SPMPST v0.2 ("naming debt", section 10).
- Do **not** move or rename `feluqa.rs/000-art/**` (published at `/art/…`, may be referenced by the front end) or any Markdown content other than what P5.6 lists.

### 1.3 Frozen contract

| Artifact | Rule |
|---|---|
| `docs/vitepress-site/.generated-guides/**` | byte-identical (exceptions: P5.6 allow-list) |
| `docs/vitepress-site/.vitepress/generated/*.json` | **semantically** identical: parsed JSON with sorted object keys; **array order must match** |
| `docs/vitepress-site/.vitepress/generated/*.ts` | byte-identical |
| Return shape of `loadSiteRuntimeContext()` | identical |
| Legacy runtime config object consumed by stage code | identical until P5.4; afterwards only path-valued keys listed in Appendix C may change |

### 1.4 Layering (the architecture this refactor creates)

```
Layer 1  SPMPST source tree      docs/{.site, src, resources}        agnostic, authored by humans
Layer 2  SPMPST site model       scripts/spmpst/config/…             agnostic loader → `model` + opaque `targets`
Layer 3  Target adapter          scripts/preparation/** + .vitepress  VitePress today; Feluqa Rust SSG later
```
The adapter turns `model + targets.vitepress` into the legacy runtime object (`runtime.mjs`, section 4.3). A future adapter reads the same model.

