## 4. Config design

### 4.1 Ownership registry (ends the "scattered" problem)

`registry.mjs` is the single source of truth. The loader rejects: a key in the wrong file (`"<key>" belongs in <owner>.site.config.json, not in <file>`), an unknown key (with a "did you mean" suggestion, Levenshtein ≤ 2, implemented inline), an unknown `*.site.config.json` name, a missing mandatory file. A top-level `$schema` key is ignored everywhere.

```js
// scripts/spmpst/config/registry.mjs
export const CONCERNS = {
  definitions: { required: true,  keys: ['site', 'subguides', 'iconFallback' /* + transitional: guidesPath, indexPath, project */] },
  lang:        { required: true,  keys: ['languages', 'fallbackLanguage', 'selector'] },
  topbar:      { required: false, keys: ['items', 'theme'] },
  collections: { required: false, keys: ['collections'] },
  appearance:  { required: false, keys: ['fonts', 'logo', 'ogImages', 'mermaid'] },
  links:       { required: false, keys: ['socialLinks'] },
  seo:         { required: false, keys: ['siteUrl', 'path', 'icon'] },
}
// Target files: .site/targets/<name>.target.config.json — loaded as opaque JSON into `targets[name]`; validated ONLY by the adapter.
// Adding a concern (e.g. "concepts") = one registry entry + one validator file. Nothing else.
```

### 4.2 Locale bundle rule

`.site/locales/<lang>.locale.json` holds **every string that depends on the language and is not attached to a single entity**. Entity names (topbar item text, collection title/description, subguide `labels`) stay **inline `{ "en": …, "fr": … }`** next to the entity.

Bundle schema (all sections required unless stated):

```jsonc
{
  "language": { "label": "English", "menuLabel": "Change language",
                "fallbackNotice": "This page is not available in {requested}. Showing the {fallback} version." },
  "ui":       { "emptyCollection": "No published content yet." },
  "search":   { /* exactly the current search.labels object for that language */ },
  "outline":  { "label": "On this page" },
  "footer":   { "message": "…", "copyright": "…" },
  "notices":  { "exploringTitle": "…", "exploring": "…", "validatedTitle": "…", "validated": "…", "fallbackTitle": "…" },
  "seo":      { "quickLinksTitle": "…", "faqTitle": "…", "quickLinks": [ … ], "faq": [ … ],
                "pageTitle": "…", "pageNavTitle": "…", "description": "…" }   // required when quickLinks or faq is non-empty (replaces hard-coded English fallbacks, D4)
}
```

### 4.3 Model → legacy runtime object (frozen consumer contract)

`runtime.mjs` (`toVitepressRuntime`) must produce **exactly** the object the stage code and `site.ts` read today. This table is the spec:

| Runtime path (legacy) | Built from |
|---|---|
| `site`, `subguides` | `definitions` |
| `languages`, `fallbackLanguage` | `lang` |
| `topbar.language` | `lang.selector` |
| `topbar.items`, `topbar.theme` | `topbar` |
| `collections` | `collections` (Phase 5: `path` is synthesized, see Appendix C) |
| `fonts`, `logo`, `ogImages`, `mermaid` | `appearance` |
| `socialLinks` | `links` |
| `languageLabels[lang]` | `bundle[lang].language.label` |
| `languageMenuLabels[lang]` | `bundle[lang].language.menuLabel` |
| `languageMenuLabel` (singular) | `bundle[defaultLang].language.menuLabel` — only if D2 finds a consumer; the splitter asserts it equals the legacy value |
| `fallbackNotices[lang]` | `bundle[lang].language.fallbackNotice` |
| `search.labels.root` | `bundle[fallbackLanguage].search` |
| `search.labels[lang]` (non-default) | `bundle[lang].search` |
| `outline.labels[lang]` | `bundle[lang].outline.label` |
| `footer[lang]` | `bundle[lang].footer` |
| `documentationNotices[lang]` | `bundle[lang].notices` |
| `seo.siteUrl`, `seo.path` | `seo` |
| `seo.locales[lang]` | `{ icon: seo.icon, ...bundle[lang].seo }` |
| `publicFiles[name]` | contents of `.site/public/<name>` (strip exactly one trailing `\n`) |
| `uiStrings[lang]` *(new key)* | `bundle[lang].ui` |
| `search.provider`, `search.miniSearch`, `search.excludePaths` | **target** `search` |
| `outline.level` | **target** `outline.level` |
| `markdown` | **target** `markdown` |
| `styles`, `theme` | **target** `styles`, `theme` |
| `outputDir` | **target** `outputDir` |
| `project.components`, `project.hooks`, `project.viteConfig` | **target** (transitional); derived from layout in Phase 5 |
| `project.iconLibrary`, `project.iconFallback`, `project.mermaidConfig` | `definitions.project` (transitional); derived from layout + `definitions.iconFallback` in Phase 5 |
| `guidesPath`, `indexPath` | `definitions` (transitional); derived (`src/guides`, `index.<fallbackLanguage>.md`) in Phase 5 |

Arrays are order-sensitive and must be preserved: `languages`, `subguides`, `topbar.items`, `collections`, `socialLinks`, `styles`, `quickLinks`, `faq`. Object key order is irrelevant (the verifier canonicalizes JSON). `uiStrings` is the **only** allowed new key (register it in `.refactor/allowed-config-diffs.json`).

> Before relying on `search.labels.root`, open `.vitepress/config/site.ts` and confirm that `root` means the default locale. If not, record the truth in `DECISIONS.md` and adjust only `runtime.mjs`, never the consumer.

