## 9. Design notes for planned features (DO NOT implement now)

### 9.1 Collection category pages
Target URLs `<base>/<collection>/<category>/<slug>`; collection definition gains `"categoryPages": true`. Impacts: `stagedPath()` for collections (category segment from frontmatter `category` or the `category.json` entry), `compile-collections.mjs` (emit `/<id>/<category>/index.md`), `collections.json` (`categoryLinks`), route-conflict check with `/<id>/<slug>`.

### 9.2 Concepts (hover definitions)
New concern `concepts` = registry entry + `concepts.site.config.json` (`{ "directory": "concepts" }`) + `src/concepts/<id>.<lang>.md`. A new stage `compile-concepts.mjs` emits `.vitepress/generated/concepts.json` (id → localized title/summary/link); a markdown-it plugin in the target wraps `[[concept-id]]` into the hover component (target-bound, under `resources/targets/vitepress/`). The SPMPST side only defines the source format and the model entry.

### 9.3 Footer links
Reserve in `links.site.config.json`:
```json
{ "socialLinks": [ … ],
  "footerLinks": [ { "title": { "en": "Product", "fr": "Produit" },
                     "items": [ { "label": { "en": "Get started", "fr": "Bien démarrer" }, "link": "/get-started/" } ] } ] }
```
Runtime path `footer.links` emitted into `site-content.json`; requires a front-end component → separate task. In this run: accept the key as optional in registry/schema, no output change when absent.

### 9.4 Feluqa Rust SSG
A second adapter consumes `model` (+ its own `.site/targets/feluqa.target.config.json`). Portability requirements recorded in SSG.md: sha256 content hashing for assets, canonical JSON, deterministic ordering (`sortNavigationEntries`), no dependency on JS regex semantics beyond the documented patterns.

