## 10. `docs/SSG.md` — required specification (P6.1)

Write in English, RFC 2119 keywords (MUST/SHOULD/MAY), SPMPST **v0.1 (draft)**. Derive every rule from the real code (`scripts/spmpst/**`, `scripts/preparation/**`); each normative rule ends with `Source: <file>#<function or section>`; anything not implemented is labelled **PLANNED**. Required outline:

1. **Purpose and scope** — what SPMPST is, who consumes it (human authors, SSG adapters), what it is not.
2. **Status and versioning** — v0.1; how breaking changes will be numbered.
3. **Terminology** — tree root, guide, subguide, section, page, collection, category, locale, bundle, concern file, target, adapter, staged tree.
4. **Layers** — the three layers of section 1.4 with a diagram.
5. **Directory layout** — the fixed layout of section 3.1 and path rules of section 3.2.
6. **Source file conventions**
   - ordering prefixes (`NNN-`, removed by `cleanDir`/`cleanFile`),
   - language suffix `name.<lang>.md` (`[a-z]{2,3}(-[A-Z]{2})?`; no suffix = default language),
   - ignored entries (dot-names, `README.md`), metadata files (`sidebar.json`, `guide.config.json`, `category.json`),
   - `index` pages and generated indexes.
7. **Frontmatter** — required keys (`icon`, `sidebarTitle`), recommended keys (`title`, `description`), collection keys (`date`, `category`), pass-through rule (unknown keys are preserved for the target), generated keys (`requestedLanguage`, `contentLanguage`, `languageFallbackNotice`, `prev`, `next`, `search`, `collection`, `wordCount`, `readingTime`, `collectionIndex`).
8. **Routing** — guide `uri` (`base`, `index`, `entry`), locale prefixing and `prefixDefaultLanguage`, route cleaning, no-slash aliases, collection routes, conflicts.
9. **Languages and fallbacks** — language policy file, locale bundles, fallback pages and notice placeholders (`{requested}`, `{fallback}`), inline localized objects and their fallback order.
10. **Collections** — `layout` (`article`|`doc`), `indexLayout` (`list`|`spotlight`), `category.json`, reading metrics (200 words/minute rule from `readingMetrics`), generated index pages.
11. **Site configuration** — every concern file (keys, types, defaults, ownership table), locale bundle schema, public files, target files (opaque), ownership/validation behavior, error format.
12. **Assets and resources** — content-hashed assets (`__docs-assets/<sha256><ext>`), allowed roots, icon library resolution (families `lucide`, `custom`, `heroicons`, `simple-icons`, name pattern, fallback), sidebar icon rule (`.svg` path vs name), flags, Mermaid config and diagram rendering (light + dark variants, automatic flowchart palette when no `classDef`), fonts.
13. **Pre-SSG processing pipeline** — the ordered stages (section 5 / Phase 3 table), what each guarantees, inputs and outputs, determinism guarantees, incremental mode (`DOCS_PREPARE_INCREMENTAL`), locking (`flock`).
14. **Output contract** — the staged portable Markdown tree and the generated data files; which are portable and which are target-specific.
15. **Target adapters** — adapter responsibilities, the model/target split, the VitePress adapter (mapping table of section 4.3), plan for the Feluqa Rust SSG adapter.
16. **Conformance** — how to check a tree (`docs:check`), how to check an implementation (snapshot comparison with canonical JSON), **PLANNED**: fixtures under a conformance directory.
17. **Planned features** — section 9 (category pages, concepts, footer links).
18. **Naming debt (candidates for v0.2)** — at least: `subguides` → `guides`, drop `subguides[].label`, `sidebarTitle` → neutral navigation title key, `topbar` → `header`, `uri.entry` meaning, `documentationNotices` → `notices`, VitePress-style frontmatter flags (`sidebar: false`, `aside: false`) → neutral layout keys.
19. **Appendix A — VitePress-isms inventory** (P6.2).
20. **Appendix B — Examples** — a minimal tree (one guide, two languages, one collection) with the exact files and the resulting staged tree.

SSG.md lives at `docs/SSG.md` (outside `src/`), so it is not published by the pipeline and needs no `icon`/`sidebarTitle`.

